{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FH57YyN8nEDbS2bogAjQ9M","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T13:31:33+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\\n\\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\\n\\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\\n\\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\\n\\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\\n\\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\\n\\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14\",\"date\":\"2026-09-01T23:29:42+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\\n\\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\\n\\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\\n\\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\\n\\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\\n\\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\\n\\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\\n\\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\\n\\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\\n\\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\\n\\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers are now named 'Edit or delete procedure' and 'Attachment actions', so the specs can no longer find them by 'Options'.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d\",\"date\":\"2026-06-19T18:51:12+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d\",\"date\":\"2026-06-09T16:10:29+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"fix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\\n\\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\\naction items.\\n\\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\\nunder O3-5709.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"sfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3568fa685f2d33a17b6fb975b089ed4b0abb5cfe\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T00:37:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"05cfbca7dbdd7488e868e1ffcb5d1ff0a00aac8b\",\"date\":\"2026-04-30T11:50:10+01:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Skengmann\",\"authorEmail\":\"tonyecotterell82@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c7c10df4f1bec30712d71b2557e3222251827436\",\"date\":\"2026-04-30T15:34:20+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Devarasetty Praneeth\",\"authorEmail\":\"89689768+praneeth622@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d92a26c2a1c087c33f22cee56bf2b07c5eb96495\",\"date\":\"2026-04-22T11:56:54-09:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5614: Fix delete-condition retry and conditions search input (#3254)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"omeri innocent\",\"authorEmail\":\"innocentomeri08@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2c514a99a75389e9ccf680a9584eb68db57a2267\",\"date\":\"2026-04-21T16:48:02+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Om Srivastava\",\"authorEmail\":\"79087911+omsrivastava512@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7fa740c199cb105713451efcc641d0a250b0ef59\",\"date\":\"2026-04-02T00:20:31+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5580: Default clinical status to active when recording a new condition (#3195)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"solomonfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7f324ebd5b575f0bbb5868d71a7245c9957eeaba\",\"date\":\"2026-03-19T16:01:47+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve drug order workspace UX (#3138)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Preserve search term when navigating back from the order form\\n- Cancel on new orders returns to drug search instead of closing the workspace\\n- Auto-focus the drug search input\\n- Hide dose section in order basket tile when dosage is null\\n- Fix conditional separators in order basket tile to avoid dangling dashes\\n- Allow long drug names to wrap instead of clipping in order basket tiles\\n- Remove redundant validation error snackbar from drug order form\\n- Remove unused imports and translation keys\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c\",\"date\":\"2026-03-09T18:30:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\\n\\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\\n\\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\\ncontinue to mean \\\"no value\\\".\\n\\nAffected layers:\\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\\n  the encounter hash table\\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \\\"Not available\\\"\\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \\\"at least one field\\\"\\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\\n\\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\\n  consistency with the rest of the patch\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1012bafec8f832c80d5557bc5e818f8e2143ee\",\"date\":\"2026-03-04T22:01:35+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Improve E2E test reliability\\n\\nReplace fragile locators and fix test infrastructure issues that cause\\nintermittent E2E failures.\\n\\nSelectors:\\n- Replace .nth(0) positional selectors with row-scoped locators\\n  (dataRow, getByRole('row').filter()) across allergies, biometrics,\\n  conditions, drug-orders, lab-orders, results-viewer, visit-note, and\\n  vitals specs\\n- Replace CSS class selectors ([class*=\\\"previewContainer\\\"]) with\\n  role-based locators in attachment preview tests\\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for form input fields in\\n  drug-orders\\n- Add role=\\\"dialog\\\" and aria-label to attachment preview component\\n  for stable test targeting\\n\\nAssertions:\\n- Replace snapshot assertions (textContent + expect) with auto-retrying\\n  Playwright assertions (toHaveText, toHaveValue) in edit-existing-visit\\n- Wrap bare .isVisible() calls with expect() in immunizations\\n- Add missing await on visitsPage.goTo() in results-viewer\\n- Remove swallowed .catch(() => {}) on assertion in attachments\\n\\nTest state:\\n- Convert module-level mutable state to per-test fixtures in\\n  drug-orders and lab-orders specs (retry/parallel safe)\\n- Use test patient fixture instead of manual creation in\\n  visit-context-navigation\\n- Add try/finally with null guards for cleanup of manually created\\n  resources\\n\\nCleanup helpers:\\n- Add response status assertions to deleteEncounter, deleteDrugOrder,\\n  deleteTestOrder (accept 200/204/400/404/500)\\n- Add ok() assertion to endVisit (accept 200/400 for already-ended\\n  visits) and getVisit\\n- Remove unnecessary empty request bodies from delete helpers\\n\\nDrug order recording:\\n- Handle environment differences where the order basket may open the\\n  drug search workspace directly or require an additional click\\n\\n* Drop status assertions from delete cleanup helpers\\n\\nDelete helpers are teardown code — they shouldn't fail the test if the\\nresource was already removed or modified by the test itself. Asserting\\non an ever-growing allowlist of status codes is effectively a no-op.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b63bf8d59ee16c4fdf7dd10f3783c4ac76e31748\",\"date\":\"2026-02-05T15:18:52+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Render em-dash separators in medication displays conditionally\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Em-dash (—) separators between medication order fields (dose, route,\\nfrequency, duration, refills, dosing instructions) were rendered\\nunconditionally, causing orphaned leading dashes when preceding fields\\nwere absent. This was most visible for free text dosing orders, where\\ndose, route, and frequency are all null.\\n\\nAdditionally, \\\"Indefinite duration\\\" was always shown when duration was\\nnull, even for free text orders where it adds no useful information\\nsince there are no structured dosing fields to contextualize it.\\n\\nFixes the separator logic in all three medication display components:\\n- medication-record (Orders widget)\\n- medications-details-table (Active/Past Medications widget)\\n- medications-summary (Past Visits widget)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3e1e88e3371df36f44d36a4872ae3745548a268b\",\"date\":\"2026-01-13T01:03:11+05:30\",\"message\":\"(test) Add unit tests for ConditionsActionMenu component (#2911)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Balkawade Sai Dipak\",\"authorEmail\":\"saibalkawade10@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"770e1f73e27c092ed296fcfef9106fc6cd7c0f8f\",\"date\":\"2026-01-10T15:49:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix wrong records being shown or modified on paginated tables (#2937)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fix critical bugs where interacting with items on page 2+ of paginated\\ntables would operate on the wrong record, causing potential data corruption\\nand patient safety issues.\\n\\nAffected components:\\n- Programs overview: Action menu edited wrong enrollment; also fixed\\n  conditional rendering to show completed programs\\n- Programs detailed summary: Improved action menu robustness\\n- Immunizations: Expanded row showed wrong vaccine details\\n- Encounters: Fixed type error and improved robustness\\n\\nRoot cause: Components were using array indices from paginated rows to\\naccess the source data array, causing index misalignment. Fixed by using\\nUUID-based Map lookups for direct access.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f48abd7f30f5a167b6b952ca4f1c8a412bde6167\",\"date\":\"2025-12-10T02:52:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Wait for section title change before expecting end time input in edit visit test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Adds a wait condition for the section title to change to \\\"Visit start and end date\\\"\\nbefore expecting the end time input to be visible. This ensures the form state has\\npropagated through useWatch and the component has re-rendered with visitStatus='past'\\nbefore looking for conditionally rendered elements.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6795a9a97968c0017c71543484e1b9ce71a5ab42\",\"date\":\"2025-12-10T02:07:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix race conditions in visit form tests and radio button interactions\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Wait for tab state change before expecting conditional elements in edit visit test\\n- Increase timeout from 10s to 15s for conditionally rendered date/time inputs\\n- Use .check({ force: true }) for radio buttons to bypass Carbon styling interception\\n- Replace synchronous textContent assertions with async .toHaveText() waits in date picker test\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6a636f08627551147d3f468619bc495e796b6bd1\",\"date\":\"2025-12-10T01:05:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Try to fix flaky test failures in drug orders and visit forms\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Use specific table selectors to avoid strict mode violations in drug order tests\\n  - Target Active Medications table with .first() to distinguish from Past Medications\\n  - Prevents ambiguity when multiple medication tables are present\\n\\n- Fix race condition in edit visit form when switching to \\\"Ended\\\" status\\n  - Wait for end time input to render before filling start time\\n  - Addresses timing issue with useWatch hook and conditional rendering\\n  - Increase timeout to 10s for form state updates\\n\\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for visit type radio buttons\\n  - Ensures proper interaction with radio button controls\\n  - Follows Playwright best practices for form inputs\\n  - More reliable than clicking arbitrary text elements\\n\\nThese changes improve test stability in CI environments where timing\\ncan be less predictable than local development.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5b34d4ef72606607fc34650b4ddc64bfa5cb9683\",\"date\":\"2025-11-28T14:11:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix potential race conditions in flaky edit-existing-visit test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Wait for visitStartDateInput before clicking the \\\"Ended\\\" tab to ensure\\n  the form is fully loaded before interaction. Fixes flaky timeout where\\n  visitStopDateInput fails to appear after clicking the tab.\\n- Wait for dropdown options to be visible before clicking to prevent race\\n  conditions when selecting location.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5806aa967f2db892be99d8ce39470ab12ae54bbb\",\"date\":\"2025-11-20T14:55:29+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix potential race condition in edit-existing-visit e2e test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"54ddf9e5ecca4dc7e239e7362158ed58ee6fbc70\",\"date\":\"2025-11-04T11:09:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use correct translation namespace in allergies list extension\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes cross-app translation namespace for the allergies list extension\\nby using the `translateFrom` function with the `moduleName` as the first\\nargument instead of the `useTranslation` hook. This ensures that the translation\\nstrings are loaded from the allergies app's namespace when the extension is\\nrendered in other apps (e.g., medications app via the `allergy-list-pills-slot`\\nextension slot).\\n\\nIt also removes unused `translateFrom` imports from conditions, lists, and\\nprograms apps.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9d9c111e7abd104fdc501421526700f45703a40c\",\"date\":\"2025-10-28T22:28:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix translation extraction and update translation keys\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Fix i18next-parser to extract default values from t() calls by using\\nthe 4th parameter (value) in the defaultValue function\\n- Add missing 'errorLoadingClinicians' translation key\\n- Update conditions overview to use 'conditions_lower' key for proper casing\\n- Improve code formatting in conditions detailed summary component\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dea33fb7d213d6f86ce8ac91c5fab691c0bc013e\",\"date\":\"2025-10-21T00:04:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Correct npm tag distribution in patch release workflow (#2808)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes two critical bugs introduced in #2804:\\n\\n1. Main branch now correctly publishes to 'next' tag\\n   - Previous logic used `'' || '-patch'` which always evaluated to '-patch'\\n   - Split publish and version steps with explicit if conditions\\n\\n2. Patch releases now tagged as 'patch' instead of defaulting to 'latest'\\n   - Added --tag patch to ci:prepublish-patch script\\n   - Prevents patch releases from overwriting stable releases\\n\\nUses canonical GitHub Actions patterns with explicit branch checks\\ninstead of string concatenation.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5de1ff84ee3b4b7872484f3d864c1bf868758128\",\"date\":\"2025-08-07T16:59:00+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add translation for Conditions active status (#2656)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Mutesasira Moses\",\"authorEmail\":\"mozzymutesa@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2b6d0edcabce999a87e7a23e3c056a3b01cae14f\",\"date\":\"2025-06-30T00:58:40+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix): Translation issues and form launch issues in clinical views (#2550)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix): Translation issues and form launch issues in clinical views\\n\\n* Fix encounter tile\\n\\n* update conditional ur to useswr\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"22bc834bb133f56c7f697ef1e2a3bff77dad3711\",\"date\":\"2025-05-02T21:55:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add specialized handling for visit note encounters in encounters table\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Adds conditional logic to handle visit note encounters in the encounters table. We already had this logic wired up in the Overflow menu, so this\\ncommit just extends it to the action buttons at the bottom of the expanded row for consistency.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2abeb8e40648ec9ec8e897b6ddb76949e9db958c\",\"date\":\"2025-04-03T01:39:48+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4584: Validate against future onset dates in the conditions form (#2326)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix: Validate onset date to ensure it cannot be in the future\\n\\n* Add translation for onset date validation message\\n\\n* Update translation key\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"praneeth\",\"authorEmail\":\"141117659+Muppasanipraneeth@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0e206391af809d9cb73a0440632d34277dff7f61\",\"date\":\"2025-03-15T20:20:35+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Improve selector reliability in conditions test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace generic text-based selector with more specific role+filter selector\\nfor selecting the \\\"All\\\" option in the conditions dropdown menu.\\nThis makes the test more precise by ensuring it clicks on the correct\\noption element rather than any element containing the text \\\"all\\\", such as the Allergies dashboard link.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fee19d055071df1e458cc3bb9a944538b5dec58f\",\"date\":\"2025-03-06T12:38:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) O3-3846: Replace Carbon datepickers with reusable `OpenmrsDatePicker` (#2154)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat/O3-3846: All Calendar Date Pickers should use the same OpenmrsDatePicker component across entire EMR\\n\\n* Add stub implementation for OpenmrsDatePicker in tests\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* fix the missing props\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* Fix the failing test\\n\\n* Remove extra code\\n\\n* fix build failure\\n\\n* Fix the failing test on Programs app\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* Refactor all OpenMRS Date picker implementations\\n\\n* Update unit tests to accomodate openmrs date picker\\n\\n* Update e2e tests\\n\\n* Fix failing e2e tests\\n\\n* Fix conditions e2e test\\n\\n* Update framework\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <sharmava05@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <neth23rodrigo@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":107}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e882a91-c39c-463a-93c4-92fdf770d306","uuid":"8dbdcd76-3658-4470-a4a5-d2c562c81582","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:58:11.060Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T13:31:33+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\\n\\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\\n\\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\\n\\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\\n\\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\\n\\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\\n\\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14\",\"date\":\"2026-09-01T23:29:42+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\\n\\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\\n\\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\\n\\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\\n\\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\\n\\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\\n\\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\\n\\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\\n\\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\\n\\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\\n\\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers are now named 'Edit or delete procedure' and 'Attachment actions', so the specs can no longer find them by 'Options'.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d\",\"date\":\"2026-06-19T18:51:12+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d\",\"date\":\"2026-06-09T16:10:29+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"fix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\\n\\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\\naction items.\\n\\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\\nunder O3-5709.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"sfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3568fa685f2d33a17b6fb975b089ed4b0abb5cfe\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T00:37:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"05cfbca7dbdd7488e868e1ffcb5d1ff0a00aac8b\",\"date\":\"2026-04-30T11:50:10+01:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Skengmann\",\"authorEmail\":\"tonyecotterell82@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c7c10df4f1bec30712d71b2557e3222251827436\",\"date\":\"2026-04-30T15:34:20+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Devarasetty Praneeth\",\"authorEmail\":\"89689768+praneeth622@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d92a26c2a1c087c33f22cee56bf2b07c5eb96495\",\"date\":\"2026-04-22T11:56:54-09:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5614: Fix delete-condition retry and conditions search input (#3254)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"omeri innocent\",\"authorEmail\":\"innocentomeri08@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2c514a99a75389e9ccf680a9584eb68db57a2267\",\"date\":\"2026-04-21T16:48:02+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Om Srivastava\",\"authorEmail\":\"79087911+omsrivastava512@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7fa740c199cb105713451efcc641d0a250b0ef59\",\"date\":\"2026-04-02T00:20:31+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5580: Default clinical status to active when recording a new condition (#3195)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"solomonfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7f324ebd5b575f0bbb5868d71a7245c9957eeaba\",\"date\":\"2026-03-19T16:01:47+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve drug order workspace UX (#3138)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Preserve search term when navigating back from the order form\\n- Cancel on new orders returns to drug search instead of closing the workspace\\n- Auto-focus the drug search input\\n- Hide dose section in order basket tile when dosage is null\\n- Fix conditional separators in order basket tile to avoid dangling dashes\\n- Allow long drug names to wrap instead of clipping in order basket tiles\\n- Remove redundant validation error snackbar from drug order form\\n- Remove unused imports and translation keys\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c\",\"date\":\"2026-03-09T18:30:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\\n\\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\\n\\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\\ncontinue to mean \\\"no value\\\".\\n\\nAffected layers:\\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\\n  the encounter hash table\\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \\\"Not available\\\"\\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \\\"at least one field\\\"\\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\\n\\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\\n  consistency with the rest of the patch\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1012bafec8f832c80d5557bc5e818f8e2143ee\",\"date\":\"2026-03-04T22:01:35+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Improve E2E test reliability\\n\\nReplace fragile locators and fix test infrastructure issues that cause\\nintermittent E2E failures.\\n\\nSelectors:\\n- Replace .nth(0) positional selectors with row-scoped locators\\n  (dataRow, getByRole('row').filter()) across allergies, biometrics,\\n  conditions, drug-orders, lab-orders, results-viewer, visit-note, and\\n  vitals specs\\n- Replace CSS class selectors ([class*=\\\"previewContainer\\\"]) with\\n  role-based locators in attachment preview tests\\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for form input fields in\\n  drug-orders\\n- Add role=\\\"dialog\\\" and aria-label to attachment preview component\\n  for stable test targeting\\n\\nAssertions:\\n- Replace snapshot assertions (textContent + expect) with auto-retrying\\n  Playwright assertions (toHaveText, toHaveValue) in edit-existing-visit\\n- Wrap bare .isVisible() calls with expect() in immunizations\\n- Add missing await on visitsPage.goTo() in results-viewer\\n- Remove swallowed .catch(() => {}) on assertion in attachments\\n\\nTest state:\\n- Convert module-level mutable state to per-test fixtures in\\n  drug-orders and lab-orders specs (retry/parallel safe)\\n- Use test patient fixture instead of manual creation in\\n  visit-context-navigation\\n- Add try/finally with null guards for cleanup of manually created\\n  resources\\n\\nCleanup helpers:\\n- Add response status assertions to deleteEncounter, deleteDrugOrder,\\n  deleteTestOrder (accept 200/204/400/404/500)\\n- Add ok() assertion to endVisit (accept 200/400 for already-ended\\n  visits) and getVisit\\n- Remove unnecessary empty request bodies from delete helpers\\n\\nDrug order recording:\\n- Handle environment differences where the order basket may open the\\n  drug search workspace directly or require an additional click\\n\\n* Drop status assertions from delete cleanup helpers\\n\\nDelete helpers are teardown code — they shouldn't fail the test if the\\nresource was already removed or modified by the test itself. Asserting\\non an ever-growing allowlist of status codes is effectively a no-op.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b63bf8d59ee16c4fdf7dd10f3783c4ac76e31748\",\"date\":\"2026-02-05T15:18:52+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Render em-dash separators in medication displays conditionally\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Em-dash (—) separators between medication order fields (dose, route,\\nfrequency, duration, refills, dosing instructions) were rendered\\nunconditionally, causing orphaned leading dashes when preceding fields\\nwere absent. This was most visible for free text dosing orders, where\\ndose, route, and frequency are all null.\\n\\nAdditionally, \\\"Indefinite duration\\\" was always shown when duration was\\nnull, even for free text orders where it adds no useful information\\nsince there are no structured dosing fields to contextualize it.\\n\\nFixes the separator logic in all three medication display components:\\n- medication-record (Orders widget)\\n- medications-details-table (Active/Past Medications widget)\\n- medications-summary (Past Visits widget)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3e1e88e3371df36f44d36a4872ae3745548a268b\",\"date\":\"2026-01-13T01:03:11+05:30\",\"message\":\"(test) Add unit tests for ConditionsActionMenu component (#2911)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Balkawade Sai Dipak\",\"authorEmail\":\"saibalkawade10@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"770e1f73e27c092ed296fcfef9106fc6cd7c0f8f\",\"date\":\"2026-01-10T15:49:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix wrong records being shown or modified on paginated tables (#2937)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fix critical bugs where interacting with items on page 2+ of paginated\\ntables would operate on the wrong record, causing potential data corruption\\nand patient safety issues.\\n\\nAffected components:\\n- Programs overview: Action menu edited wrong enrollment; also fixed\\n  conditional rendering to show completed programs\\n- Programs detailed summary: Improved action menu robustness\\n- Immunizations: Expanded row showed wrong vaccine details\\n- Encounters: Fixed type error and improved robustness\\n\\nRoot cause: Components were using array indices from paginated rows to\\naccess the source data array, causing index misalignment. Fixed by using\\nUUID-based Map lookups for direct access.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f48abd7f30f5a167b6b952ca4f1c8a412bde6167\",\"date\":\"2025-12-10T02:52:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Wait for section title change before expecting end time input in edit visit test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Adds a wait condition for the section title to change to \\\"Visit start and end date\\\"\\nbefore expecting the end time input to be visible. This ensures the form state has\\npropagated through useWatch and the component has re-rendered with visitStatus='past'\\nbefore looking for conditionally rendered elements.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6795a9a97968c0017c71543484e1b9ce71a5ab42\",\"date\":\"2025-12-10T02:07:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix race conditions in visit form tests and radio button interactions\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Wait for tab state change before expecting conditional elements in edit visit test\\n- Increase timeout from 10s to 15s for conditionally rendered date/time inputs\\n- Use .check({ force: true }) for radio buttons to bypass Carbon styling interception\\n- Replace synchronous textContent assertions with async .toHaveText() waits in date picker test\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6a636f08627551147d3f468619bc495e796b6bd1\",\"date\":\"2025-12-10T01:05:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Try to fix flaky test failures in drug orders and visit forms\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Use specific table selectors to avoid strict mode violations in drug order tests\\n  - Target Active Medications table with .first() to distinguish from Past Medications\\n  - Prevents ambiguity when multiple medication tables are present\\n\\n- Fix race condition in edit visit form when switching to \\\"Ended\\\" status\\n  - Wait for end time input to render before filling start time\\n  - Addresses timing issue with useWatch hook and conditional rendering\\n  - Increase timeout to 10s for form state updates\\n\\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for visit type radio buttons\\n  - Ensures proper interaction with radio button controls\\n  - Follows Playwright best practices for form inputs\\n  - More reliable than clicking arbitrary text elements\\n\\nThese changes improve test stability in CI environments where timing\\ncan be less predictable than local development.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5b34d4ef72606607fc34650b4ddc64bfa5cb9683\",\"date\":\"2025-11-28T14:11:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix potential race conditions in flaky edit-existing-visit test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Wait for visitStartDateInput before clicking the \\\"Ended\\\" tab to ensure\\n  the form is fully loaded before interaction. Fixes flaky timeout where\\n  visitStopDateInput fails to appear after clicking the tab.\\n- Wait for dropdown options to be visible before clicking to prevent race\\n  conditions when selecting location.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5806aa967f2db892be99d8ce39470ab12ae54bbb\",\"date\":\"2025-11-20T14:55:29+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix potential race condition in edit-existing-visit e2e test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"54ddf9e5ecca4dc7e239e7362158ed58ee6fbc70\",\"date\":\"2025-11-04T11:09:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use correct translation namespace in allergies list extension\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes cross-app translation namespace for the allergies list extension\\nby using the `translateFrom` function with the `moduleName` as the first\\nargument instead of the `useTranslation` hook. This ensures that the translation\\nstrings are loaded from the allergies app's namespace when the extension is\\nrendered in other apps (e.g., medications app via the `allergy-list-pills-slot`\\nextension slot).\\n\\nIt also removes unused `translateFrom` imports from conditions, lists, and\\nprograms apps.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9d9c111e7abd104fdc501421526700f45703a40c\",\"date\":\"2025-10-28T22:28:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix translation extraction and update translation keys\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Fix i18next-parser to extract default values from t() calls by using\\nthe 4th parameter (value) in the defaultValue function\\n- Add missing 'errorLoadingClinicians' translation key\\n- Update conditions overview to use 'conditions_lower' key for proper casing\\n- Improve code formatting in conditions detailed summary component\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dea33fb7d213d6f86ce8ac91c5fab691c0bc013e\",\"date\":\"2025-10-21T00:04:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Correct npm tag distribution in patch release workflow (#2808)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes two critical bugs introduced in #2804:\\n\\n1. Main branch now correctly publishes to 'next' tag\\n   - Previous logic used `'' || '-patch'` which always evaluated to '-patch'\\n   - Split publish and version steps with explicit if conditions\\n\\n2. Patch releases now tagged as 'patch' instead of defaulting to 'latest'\\n   - Added --tag patch to ci:prepublish-patch script\\n   - Prevents patch releases from overwriting stable releases\\n\\nUses canonical GitHub Actions patterns with explicit branch checks\\ninstead of string concatenation.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5de1ff84ee3b4b7872484f3d864c1bf868758128\",\"date\":\"2025-08-07T16:59:00+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add translation for Conditions active status (#2656)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Mutesasira Moses\",\"authorEmail\":\"mozzymutesa@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2b6d0edcabce999a87e7a23e3c056a3b01cae14f\",\"date\":\"2025-06-30T00:58:40+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix): Translation issues and form launch issues in clinical views (#2550)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix): Translation issues and form launch issues in clinical views\\n\\n* Fix encounter tile\\n\\n* update conditional ur to useswr\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"22bc834bb133f56c7f697ef1e2a3bff77dad3711\",\"date\":\"2025-05-02T21:55:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add specialized handling for visit note encounters in encounters table\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Adds conditional logic to handle visit note encounters in the encounters table. We already had this logic wired up in the Overflow menu, so this\\ncommit just extends it to the action buttons at the bottom of the expanded row for consistency.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2abeb8e40648ec9ec8e897b6ddb76949e9db958c\",\"date\":\"2025-04-03T01:39:48+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4584: Validate against future onset dates in the conditions form (#2326)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix: Validate onset date to ensure it cannot be in the future\\n\\n* Add translation for onset date validation message\\n\\n* Update translation key\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"praneeth\",\"authorEmail\":\"141117659+Muppasanipraneeth@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0e206391af809d9cb73a0440632d34277dff7f61\",\"date\":\"2025-03-15T20:20:35+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Improve selector reliability in conditions test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace generic text-based selector with more specific role+filter selector\\nfor selecting the \\\"All\\\" option in the conditions dropdown menu.\\nThis makes the test more precise by ensuring it clicks on the correct\\noption element rather than any element containing the text \\\"all\\\", such as the Allergies dashboard link.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fee19d055071df1e458cc3bb9a944538b5dec58f\",\"date\":\"2025-03-06T12:38:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) O3-3846: Replace Carbon datepickers with reusable `OpenmrsDatePicker` (#2154)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat/O3-3846: All Calendar Date Pickers should use the same OpenmrsDatePicker component across entire EMR\\n\\n* Add stub implementation for OpenmrsDatePicker in tests\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* fix the missing props\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* Fix the failing test\\n\\n* Remove extra code\\n\\n* fix build failure\\n\\n* Fix the failing test on Programs app\\n\\n* Code refactor\\n\\n* Refactor all OpenMRS Date picker implementations\\n\\n* Update unit tests to accomodate openmrs date picker\\n\\n* Update e2e tests\\n\\n* Fix failing e2e tests\\n\\n* Fix conditions e2e test\\n\\n* Update framework\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <sharmava05@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <neth23rodrigo@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":107}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FH57YyN8nEDbS2bogAjQ9M","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
