{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKbuEoYKPbYumNmsJGRq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SyejwAzx1ncx1fcSzZLbMn","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","query":"diagnos","perPage":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1327,"cache_read_input_tokens":26017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1327},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e882a91-c39c-463a-93c4-92fdf770d306","uuid":"30bee584-7ff1-47ca-b92c-f1fe98db1816","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:58:17.572Z","request_id":"req_011CgKbuESxZ3VB9vNTAiAgz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SyejwAzx1ncx1fcSzZLbMn":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","query":"diagnos","perPage":30}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SyejwAzx1ncx1fcSzZLbMn","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SyejwAzx1ncx1fcSzZLbMn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T16:20:03+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee\",\"authorEmail\":\"veronica.mukuhi@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23\",\"date\":\"2026-09-24T18:31:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"By the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\\nshowed \\\"Error saving visit note\\\" and left the form open in create mode, so\\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\\n\\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\\nthe error and keeps the form open.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-23T11:32:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\\n\\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\\n\\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\\n\\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\\n\\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\\n\\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\\n\\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\\n\\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\\n\\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\\n\\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\\n\\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25\",\"date\":\"2026-09-12T00:11:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\\n\\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\\n\\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\\n\\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\\n\\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\\n\\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\\n\\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\\n\\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\\n\\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T22:50:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T13:38:00+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\\nto the yarn up list lets the existing automation open the catch-up PR\\nand keep the Angular engine current alongside its React peer.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e9b29360b21e0e0db589259b64f1ea4840f7f542\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T10:21:41+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The Angular form engine passes a diagnosis question's schema-level\\ndatasource config (datasource.config, including conceptSourceUuid) to\\nsearchOptions and resolveSelectedValue. The diagnoses datasource\\npreviously ignored it, so no terminology code could be displayed next\\nto a diagnosis.\\n\\n- findDiagnoses and resolveConcept accept an optional dataSourceOptions\\n  argument. When it names a conceptSourceUuid, the concept search and\\n  the selected-value lookup request conceptMappings in the rep and emit\\n  a code field on the option, so the picker can render\\n  \\\"{ICD11CODE} {Name}\\\" per the KNHTS convention.\\n- The code comes from the concept's mapping to the configured source,\\n  preferring SAME-AS mappings over other map types.\\n- Concepts without a mapping to the source, and questions without the\\n  config, behave exactly as before. Other datasources that share\\n  mapConcept and resolveConcept are unchanged.\\n\\nCompanion to openmrs/openmrs-ngx-formentry#176, which renders the code\\nfield.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a54ee18edf3e20ce91dee366c708794e027693ef\",\"date\":\"2025-11-26T12:40:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Add coverage for optional primary diagnosis and improve config documentation\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Test changes:\\n- Add tests for `isPrimaryDiagnosisRequired` configuration behavior\\n- Test visit note submission without diagnosis when config is false\\n- Test validation enforcement when config is true\\n- Remove unused `errorMessage` variable\\n\\nConfig improvements:\\n- Add missing descriptions for all visit note config properties\\n- Fix `formConceptUuid` type from `ConceptUuid` to `UUID`\\n- Improve `diagnosisConceptClass` description for clarity\\n\\nRelated to #2836\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9a03195cbb1d7c9d720e97ed2f1b2e0b9a7eb7fd\",\"date\":\"2025-11-26T09:43:42+01:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add possibility to make primary diagnosis optional (#2836)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add possibility to make primary diagnosis optional\\n\\n* (fix) Remove length from the dep array\",\"authorName\":\"Oliver Lewandowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"109145288+olewandowski1@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4687dfc6c03e3b0bca9139f076b2a7f6235a7bd2\",\"date\":\"2025-05-02T14:54:20+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-4038: Add edit capability to visit notes form (#2412)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add edit capability to visit notes form\\n\\nThis PR adds support for editing existing visit notes. It does so by extending the existing visit notes form to support editing, and adding new API endpoints for updating visit notes and diagnoses. It also updates the visit note form test suite to cover the new functionality.\\n\\n* Review feedback\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c3cf478c051c5508c806eb93ece78e40995f31f3\",\"date\":\"2025-03-27T00:24:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Simplify secondary diagnosis selection in visit note e2e test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This commit simplifies the secondary diagnosis selection in the visit\\nnote e2e test by setting a diagnosis with a shorter name. Previously, we set\\n'Infection by Ascaris Lumbricoides' as the secondary diagnosis. This is a\\nfairly long name and it was causing issues with the test. More specifically, in newer versions\\nof Carbon, when a long name is set, the Tag component will truncate the text and display a tooltip.\\nThe presence of the tooltip was causing the test to fail because Playwright would\\nencounter a strict mode violation.\\n\\nBy setting the secondary diagnosis to 'GI upset', we avoid this issue and the test\\npasses consistently.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eeb8b91291a34af3bccec08511dc976f2d15050d\",\"date\":\"2025-01-14T13:39:07+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4302: Hide voided diagnoses in patient chart visits widget (#2167)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-4302 Hide voided diagnosis in visits widget on patient chart\\r\\n\\r\\n* code review\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"CynthiaKamau\",\"authorEmail\":\"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5b806ce76a8139936f6d5ea9b6c38e4e9017317a\",\"date\":\"2024-12-09T22:54:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) Use concept resource for conditions search (#2143)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (refactor) Use concept resource for conditions search\\r\\n\\r\\nPresently, we are using the [conceptsearch resource](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/blob/main/packages/esm-patient-conditions-app/src/conditions/conditions.resource.ts#L109) to do a lookup for conditions in the Conditions form. This is different from what we do in the Visit note form’s diagnosis search fields where we use the [concept resource](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/blob/main/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes.resource.ts#L106) with a fuzzy search.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne undesired side effect of using conceptsearch as we’re currently using it is that cross-locale searches don’t work. If the locale is set to fr for example, you can only search using the french names for a condition. So searching for malaria in the Condition search field won’t return anything, you’d have to search for paludisme.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe should use the concept resource with a fuzzy search for the Conditions form as well for a consistent search experience.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Move search results rendering into a separate component\\r\\n\\r\\nMoves the search results rendering logic from an IIFE to a dedicated SearchResults component. This improves code readability and maintainability by better separating concerns. It also fixes a rendering issue where clearing the search field would lead to the last search result being displayed.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"91f6c058c417536129086e2e49a206752a814038\",\"date\":\"2024-10-17T11:50:54+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-4088: Sort diagnoses tags in visit summary by rank (#2064)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat: sort diagnoses by order\\r\\n\\r\\n* feat: sort diagnoses by rank\\r\\n\\r\\n* add suggestions\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\r\\n\\r\\n* add tests\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Usama Idriss Kakumba\",\"authorEmail\":\"53287480+usamaidrsk@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4bc6610cbd4a91e00032c5cd5215c51a591afea2\",\"date\":\"2024-05-14T20:36:17+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-3196: Fix diagnoses tags display on tablet (#1834)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"723665795d0b16de5d04f21685f2042a3326f214\",\"date\":\"2024-03-19T16:30:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove unnecessary param from diagnosis search request\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"974abc641304ba9427d65b57fc3e68fae14b8f31\",\"date\":\"2024-03-19T00:53:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Only show concepts diagnoses concepts in visit notes diagnosis search (#1742)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* exclusively fetch diagnosis information when populating primary and secondary diagnoses in the 'Add Noted' widget\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Kalungi Deborah\",\"authorEmail\":\"kalungi2k6@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e52c2e74ff9a3924941acf91252dfd892a72e8bf\",\"date\":\"2024-02-13T16:37:26+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-2832 : Implemented validation check for Primary Diagnosis and Secondary Diagnosis in visit-note (#1647)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix(visit-note) : Implemented validation check for diagnosis input\\r\\n\\r\\n* refactor(visit-note) : Refactor diagnosis selection logic in VisitNotesForm component\",\"authorName\":\"SENTHIL ATHIBAN M\",\"authorEmail\":\"93466587+senthil-k8s@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7a49ac26795b571004a5c1a581dbe6358019f0d1\",\"date\":\"2023-12-01T15:06:51-05:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Make it so visit diagnosis error doesn't crash the app (#1521)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Brandon Istenes\",\"authorEmail\":\"bistenes@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"843f8adeb7f0669a678b5d7939104c2675bd11c0\",\"date\":\"2023-04-18T15:01:39-04:00\",\"message\":\"Revert \\\"Added diagnoses support to formentry (#991)\\\"\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian_bacher@brown.edu\"},{\"hash\":\"af1d06020b91c4d6dc24c3ef4ce406382764124d\",\"date\":\"2023-04-17T15:17:09+01:00\",\"message\":\"Added diagnoses support to formentry (#991)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"icrc-loliveira\",\"authorEmail\":\"68058940+icrc-loliveira@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"17279569cc0c4e45cc45586f31e458c6dc7fa25d\",\"date\":\"2022-11-11T20:35:52Z\",\"message\":\"Restore normal display to diagnoses in past-visits-component (#857)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Restore normal display to diagnoses in past-visits-component\\r\\n\\r\\n* Change mock data to match new development\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Andre Gomes <Andre.Gomes@emea.merkleinc.com>\",\"authorName\":\"icrc-agomes\",\"authorEmail\":\"106243905+icrc-agomes@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a3dfe67eeea0e96cfb822ca07fe2f33d5806f30b\",\"date\":\"2022-09-26T15:09:00+01:00\",\"message\":\"O3-1281: Visit Note - Add Ability to Mark Primary and Secondary Diagnoses (#757)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"icrc-loliveira\",\"authorEmail\":\"68058940+icrc-loliveira@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1aba5e5af295a235cc10ba4ee60dde18807a876c\",\"date\":\"2022-02-16T22:45:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"O3-1105: Visit notes widget should only display visit note data (#555)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* O3-1105: Visit notes widget should only display visit note data\\r\\n\\r\\nPresently, the visit notes widget displays data about encounters. This widget should instead show data from a visit note, including:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Any recorded diagnoses.\\r\\n- Any recorded visit notes.\\r\\n- The date of capture of the information.\\r\\n\\r\\nLink to Ciaran's design QA which flagged this anomaly - https://www.notion.so/Patient-Summary-7e91d9b019a24e07b27301aa8164c323\\r\\n\\r\\nRelevant Zeplin screen - https://app.zeplin.io/project/60d59321e8100b0324762e05/screen/60d5e3accb92fbbaeb9e6edc\\r\\n\\r\\n* Update `formatDate` signature\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6a802ce23281747a0682ef0d298ab5247130b408\",\"date\":\"2022-01-11T01:56:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"Typeahead visual fixes (#494)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Applies some UI fixes to the typeahead search inputs for conditions and diagnoses. These include:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Use of a border around the search results container to distinguish it visually from the rest of the form content.\\r\\n- Use of enough padding for each search result so that the last visible result gets partially hidden from view. The hope is that this makes it apparent to the user that the results container is scrollable. I'm keen to hear if a different approach would work better here.\\r\\n- Making the conditions search input in the `Conditions` form full-width. Constraining it to just 50% of the viewport meant search results with long names aren't instantly parseable on first viewing. Full-width might be too wide but it certainly looks better than half-width.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9970d8a5de8c2f6fc594f68806088df1680d867b\",\"date\":\"2021-06-09T17:24:21+05:30\",\"message\":\"Base Structure for Past Visits Widget. (#276)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Base Structure for Past Visits Widget.\\r\\n\\r\\n* BMinor fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added Observations for every Encounter in expanded form\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed Console statements\\r\\n\\r\\n* Code Cleanup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added SkeletonText in Loading Observations for an encounter\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added SkeletonText while loading Visits\\r\\n\\r\\n* Completed Encounter List and Basic structure of Visit Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n* Completed Medications in the Visit Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n* Split components into different files\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changed the order for fetching observations and completed Diagnoses as well.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Completed notes tab and added provider in the medications\\r\\n\\r\\n* Tried adding Interfaces for all the used Variables\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Single Column in Visits\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes reviewed by Dennis\\r\\n\\r\\n* Intermidiate commit, might reverse it later\\r\\n\\r\\n* Final Design changes completed\\r\\n\\r\\n* CSS fixups\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor fixups in expanded row\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes required by Dennis\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor final fixups and seprated visit detail component\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes in translations\\r\\n\\r\\n* Final changes, visually reviewed by Ciaran.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Empty state for tests added.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Content switcher fixed\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor Fixes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes in Order Interface, Observation Interface and corrected getDosage in visit.resource\\r\\n\\r\\n* extract visit test-results to extension slot\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes required by Florian\\r\\n\\r\\n* finish moving test results extension prop types\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes required completed.\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Nikita Malyschkin <nikita.malyschkin@googlemail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Vineet Sharma\",\"authorEmail\":\"51502471+vasharma05@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7f4a9043523ea366d184dae33ecd078ba2311260\",\"date\":\"2021-06-06T22:05:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"Visit notes form enhancements (#281)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Visit notes form enhancements\\r\\n\\r\\n- Verify that an active visit is ongoing before launching the form. If there's no active visit, prompt the user to start a visit.\\r\\n- Use a state machine to more reliably handle the various form states and transitions. This fixes an issue where the user could submit an empty form.\\r\\n- Show an error toast if there is a problem submitting the form.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Add translation for submission error\\r\\n\\r\\n* Respond to review feedback\\r\\n\\r\\n* Make diagnosis search results panel scrollable\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7f7b2ed6ec0f6ea007830d4be2e0444305b02388\",\"date\":\"2021-05-02T23:10:13+03:00\",\"message\":\"Enhancements to the visit notes form (#238)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Use correct slot name in the attach function that launches the workspace.\\r\\n- Add transation keys and their corresponding strings.\\r\\n- Amend empty results pane to show the search query in addition to the error message.\\r\\n- Small changes to the rendering logic for the diagnosis search field.\\r\\n- Display a toast with a success message upon successfully saving a visit note.\\r\\n- Memoize debounced search function.\\r\\n- Improved type annotations.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":28}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e882a91-c39c-463a-93c4-92fdf770d306","uuid":"a494d7d5-1d97-461e-9d9b-f3564d8f6feb","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:58:17.699Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T16:20:03+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee\",\"authorEmail\":\"veronica.mukuhi@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23\",\"date\":\"2026-09-24T18:31:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"By the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\\nshowed \\\"Error saving visit note\\\" and left the form open in create mode, so\\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\\n\\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\\nthe error and keeps the form open.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-23T11:32:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\\n\\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\\n\\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\\n\\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\\n\\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\\n\\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\\n\\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\\n\\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\\n\\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\\n\\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\\n\\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25\",\"date\":\"2026-09-12T00:11:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\\n\\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\\n\\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\\n\\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\\n\\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\\n\\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\\n\\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\\n\\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\\n\\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T22:50:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T13:38:00+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\\nto the yarn up list lets the existing automation open the catch-up PR\\nand keep the Angular engine current alongside its React peer.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e9b29360b21e0e0db589259b64f1ea4840f7f542\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T10:21:41+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The Angular form engine passes a diagnosis question's schema-level\\ndatasource config (datasource.config, including conceptSourceUuid) to\\nsearchOptions and resolveSelectedValue. The diagnoses datasource\\npreviously ignored it, so no terminology code could be displayed next\\nto a diagnosis.\\n\\n- findDiagnoses and resolveConcept accept an optional dataSourceOptions\\n  argument. When it names a conceptSourceUuid, the concept search and\\n  the selected-value lookup request conceptMappings in the rep and emit\\n  a code field on the option, so the picker can render\\n  \\\"{ICD11CODE} {Name}\\\" per the KNHTS convention.\\n- The code comes from the concept's mapping to the configured source,\\n  preferring SAME-AS mappings over other map types.\\n- Concepts without a mapping to the source, and questions without the\\n  config, behave exactly as before. Other datasources that share\\n  mapConcept and resolveConcept are unchanged.\\n\\nCompanion to openmrs/openmrs-ngx-formentry#176, which renders the code\\nfield.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a54ee18edf3e20ce91dee366c708794e027693ef\",\"date\":\"2025-11-26T12:40:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Add coverage for optional primary diagnosis and improve config documentation\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Test changes:\\n- Add tests for `isPrimaryDiagnosisRequired` configuration behavior\\n- Test visit note submission without diagnosis when config is false\\n- Test validation enforcement when config is true\\n- Remove unused `errorMessage` variable\\n\\nConfig improvements:\\n- Add missing descriptions for all visit note config properties\\n- Fix `formConceptUuid` type from `ConceptUuid` to `UUID`\\n- Improve `diagnosisConceptClass` description for clarity\\n\\nRelated to #2836\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9a03195cbb1d7c9d720e97ed2f1b2e0b9a7eb7fd\",\"date\":\"2025-11-26T09:43:42+01:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add possibility to make primary diagnosis optional (#2836)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add possibility to make primary diagnosis optional\\n\\n* (fix) Remove length from the dep array\",\"authorName\":\"Oliver Lewandowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"109145288+olewandowski1@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4687dfc6c03e3b0bca9139f076b2a7f6235a7bd2\",\"date\":\"2025-05-02T14:54:20+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-4038: Add edit capability to visit notes form (#2412)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add edit capability to visit notes form\\n\\nThis PR adds support for editing existing visit notes. It does so by extending the existing visit notes form to support editing, and adding new API endpoints for updating visit notes and diagnoses. It also updates the visit note form test suite to cover the new functionality.\\n\\n* Review feedback\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c3cf478c051c5508c806eb93ece78e40995f31f3\",\"date\":\"2025-03-27T00:24:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Simplify secondary diagnosis selection in visit note e2e test\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This commit simplifies the secondary diagnosis selection in the visit\\nnote e2e test by setting a diagnosis with a shorter name. Previously, we set\\n'Infection by Ascaris Lumbricoides' as the secondary diagnosis. This is a\\nfairly long name and it was causing issues with the test. More specifically, in newer versions\\nof Carbon, when a long name is set, the Tag component will truncate the text and display a tooltip.\\nThe presence of the tooltip was causing the test to fail because Playwright would\\nencounter a strict mode violation.\\n\\nBy setting the secondary diagnosis to 'GI upset', we avoid this issue and the test\\npasses consistently.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eeb8b91291a34af3bccec08511dc976f2d15050d\",\"date\":\"2025-01-14T13:39:07+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4302: Hide voided diagnoses in patient chart visits widget (#2167)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-4302 Hide voided diagnosis in visits widget on patient chart\\r\\n\\r\\n* code review\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"CynthiaKamau\",\"authorEmail\":\"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5b806ce76a8139936f6d5ea9b6c38e4e9017317a\",\"date\":\"2024-12-09T22:54:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(refactor) Use concept resource for conditions search (#2143)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (refactor) Use concept resource for conditions search\\r\\n\\r\\nPresently, we are using the [conceptsearch resource](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/blob/main/packages/esm-patient-conditions-app/src/conditions/conditions.resource.ts#L109) to do a lookup for conditions in the Conditions form. This is different from what we do in the Visit note form’s diagnosis search fields where we use the [concept resource](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/blob/main/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes.resource.ts#L106) with a fuzzy search.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne undesired side effect of using conceptsearch as we’re currently using it is that cross-locale searches don’t work. If the locale is set to fr for example, you can only search using the french names for a condition. So searching for malaria in the Condition search field won’t return anything, you’d have to search for paludisme.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe should use the concept resource with a fuzzy search for the Conditions form as well for a consistent search experience.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Move search results rendering into a separate component\\r\\n\\r\\nMoves the search results rendering logic from an IIFE to a dedicated SearchResults component. This improves code readability and maintainability by better separating concerns. It also fixes a rendering issue where clearing the search field would lead to the last search result being displayed.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"91f6c058c417536129086e2e49a206752a814038\",\"date\":\"2024-10-17T11:50:54+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-4088: Sort diagnoses tags in visit summary by rank (#2064)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* feat: sort diagnoses by order\\r\\n\\r\\n* feat: sort diagnoses by rank\\r\\n\\r\\n* add suggestions\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\r\\n\\r\\n* add tests\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Usama Idriss Kakumba\",\"authorEmail\":\"53287480+usamaidrsk@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4bc6610cbd4a91e00032c5cd5215c51a591afea2\",\"date\":\"2024-05-14T20:36:17+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-3196: Fix diagnoses tags display on tablet (#1834)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"723665795d0b16de5d04f21685f2042a3326f214\",\"date\":\"2024-03-19T16:30:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove unnecessary param from diagnosis search request\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"974abc641304ba9427d65b57fc3e68fae14b8f31\",\"date\":\"2024-03-19T00:53:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Only show concepts diagnoses concepts in visit notes diagnosis search (#1742)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* exclusively fetch diagnosis information when populating primary and secondary diagnoses in the 'Add Noted' widget\\r\\n\\r\\n* Fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n---------\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Kalungi Deborah\",\"authorEmail\":\"kalungi2k6@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e52c2e74ff9a3924941acf91252dfd892a72e8bf\",\"date\":\"2024-02-13T16:37:26+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-2832 : Implemented validation check for Primary Diagnosis and Secondary Diagnosis in visit-note (#1647)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix(visit-note) : Implemented validation check for diagnosis input\\r\\n\\r\\n* refactor(visit-note) : Refactor diagnosis selection logic in VisitNotesForm component\",\"authorName\":\"SENTHIL ATHIBAN M\",\"authorEmail\":\"93466587+senthil-k8s@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7a49ac26795b571004a5c1a581dbe6358019f0d1\",\"date\":\"2023-12-01T15:06:51-05:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Make it so visit diagnosis error doesn't crash the app (#1521)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Brandon Istenes\",\"authorEmail\":\"bistenes@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"843f8adeb7f0669a678b5d7939104c2675bd11c0\",\"date\":\"2023-04-18T15:01:39-04:00\",\"message\":\"Revert \\\"Added diagnoses support to formentry (#991)\\\"\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian_bacher@brown.edu\"},{\"hash\":\"af1d06020b91c4d6dc24c3ef4ce406382764124d\",\"date\":\"2023-04-17T15:17:09+01:00\",\"message\":\"Added diagnoses support to formentry (#991)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"icrc-loliveira\",\"authorEmail\":\"68058940+icrc-loliveira@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"17279569cc0c4e45cc45586f31e458c6dc7fa25d\",\"date\":\"2022-11-11T20:35:52Z\",\"message\":\"Restore normal display to diagnoses in past-visits-component (#857)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Restore normal display to diagnoses in past-visits-component\\r\\n\\r\\n* Change mock data to match new development\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Andre Gomes <Andre.Gomes@emea.merkleinc.com>\",\"authorName\":\"icrc-agomes\",\"authorEmail\":\"106243905+icrc-agomes@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a3dfe67eeea0e96cfb822ca07fe2f33d5806f30b\",\"date\":\"2022-09-26T15:09:00+01:00\",\"message\":\"O3-1281: Visit Note - Add Ability to Mark Primary and Secondary Diagnoses (#757)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"icrc-loliveira\",\"authorEmail\":\"68058940+icrc-loliveira@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1aba5e5af295a235cc10ba4ee60dde18807a876c\",\"date\":\"2022-02-16T22:45:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"O3-1105: Visit notes widget should only display visit note data (#555)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* O3-1105: Visit notes widget should only display visit note data\\r\\n\\r\\nPresently, the visit notes widget displays data about encounters. This widget should instead show data from a visit note, including:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Any recorded diagnoses.\\r\\n- Any recorded visit notes.\\r\\n- The date of capture of the information.\\r\\n\\r\\nLink to Ciaran's design QA which flagged this anomaly - https://www.notion.so/Patient-Summary-7e91d9b019a24e07b27301aa8164c323\\r\\n\\r\\nRelevant Zeplin screen - https://app.zeplin.io/project/60d59321e8100b0324762e05/screen/60d5e3accb92fbbaeb9e6edc\\r\\n\\r\\n* Update `formatDate` signature\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6a802ce23281747a0682ef0d298ab5247130b408\",\"date\":\"2022-01-11T01:56:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"Typeahead visual fixes (#494)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Applies some UI fixes to the typeahead search inputs for conditions and diagnoses. These include:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Use of a border around the search results container to distinguish it visually from the rest of the form content.\\r\\n- Use of enough padding for each search result so that the last visible result gets partially hidden from view. The hope is that this makes it apparent to the user that the results container is scrollable. I'm keen to hear if a different approach would work better here.\\r\\n- Making the conditions search input in the `Conditions` form full-width. Constraining it to just 50% of the viewport meant search results with long names aren't instantly parseable on first viewing. Full-width might be too wide but it certainly looks better than half-width.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9970d8a5de8c2f6fc594f68806088df1680d867b\",\"date\":\"2021-06-09T17:24:21+05:30\",\"message\":\"Base Structure for Past Visits Widget. (#276)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Base Structure for Past Visits Widget.\\r\\n\\r\\n* BMinor fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added Observations for every Encounter in expanded form\\r\\n\\r\\n* Removed Console statements\\r\\n\\r\\n* Code Cleanup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added SkeletonText in Loading Observations for an encounter\\r\\n\\r\\n* Added SkeletonText while loading Visits\\r\\n\\r\\n* Completed Encounter List and Basic structure of Visit Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n* Completed Medications in the Visit Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n* Split components into different files\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changed the order for fetching observations and completed Diagnoses as well.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Completed notes tab and added provider in the medications\\r\\n\\r\\n* Tried adding Interfaces for all the used Variables\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor fixup\\r\\n\\r\\n* Single Column in Visits\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes reviewed by Dennis\\r\\n\\r\\n* Intermidiate commit, might reverse it later\\r\\n\\r\\n* Final Design changes completed\\r\\n\\r\\n* CSS fixups\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor fixups in expanded row\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes required by Dennis\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor final fixups and seprated visit detail component\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes in translations\\r\\n\\r\\n* Final changes, visually reviewed by Ciaran.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Empty state for tests added.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Content switcher fixed\\r\\n\\r\\n* Minor Fixes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes in Order Interface, Observation Interface and corrected getDosage in visit.resource\\r\\n\\r\\n* extract visit test-results to extension slot\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes required by Florian\\r\\n\\r\\n* finish moving test results extension prop types\\r\\n\\r\\n* Changes required completed.\\r\\n\\r\\nCo-authored-by: Nikita Malyschkin <nikita.malyschkin@googlemail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Vineet Sharma\",\"authorEmail\":\"51502471+vasharma05@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7f4a9043523ea366d184dae33ecd078ba2311260\",\"date\":\"2021-06-06T22:05:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"Visit notes form enhancements (#281)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Visit notes form enhancements\\r\\n\\r\\n- Verify that an active visit is ongoing before launching the form. If there's no active visit, prompt the user to start a visit.\\r\\n- Use a state machine to more reliably handle the various form states and transitions. This fixes an issue where the user could submit an empty form.\\r\\n- Show an error toast if there is a problem submitting the form.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Add translation for submission error\\r\\n\\r\\n* Respond to review feedback\\r\\n\\r\\n* Make diagnosis search results panel scrollable\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7f7b2ed6ec0f6ea007830d4be2e0444305b02388\",\"date\":\"2021-05-02T23:10:13+03:00\",\"message\":\"Enhancements to the visit notes form (#238)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"- Use correct slot name in the attach function that launches the workspace.\\r\\n- Add transation keys and their corresponding strings.\\r\\n- Amend empty results pane to show the search query in addition to the error message.\\r\\n- Small changes to the rendering logic for the diagnosis search field.\\r\\n- Display a toast with a success message upon successfully saving a visit note.\\r\\n- Memoize debounced search function.\\r\\n- Improved type annotations.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":28}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SyejwAzx1ncx1fcSzZLbMn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
